msgid "The Market Day"
msgstr "Le jour du marché"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/014_the_market_day/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The great market day is soon! The first trader with new honey and goat's cheese gets the best "
"place. Gunnhild from the Long Lake wants it too. Can you beat her?"
msgstr ""
"Le grand jour du marché approche ! Le premier marchand qui arrive avec du miel nouveau et du "
"fromage de chèvre aura la meilleure place. Gunnhild du Long Lac la veut aussi. {crew|Peux-tu|Peux-"
"tu|Pouvez-vous} arriver avant elle ?"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/014_the_market_day/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Two crates of honey! Now the cheese."
msgstr "Deux caisses de miel ! Maintenant, le fromage."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/014_the_market_day/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Honey and cheese, and before Gunnhild! She laughs and says: next time I win. I think you two will "
"be friends."
msgstr ""
"Le miel et le fromage, et avant Gunnhild ! Elle rit et dit : la prochaine fois, c'est moi qui "
"gagne. Je crois que {crew|elle et toi, vous serez amis|elle et toi, vous serez amies|vous serez "
"tous amis|vous serez toutes amies}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/014_the_market_day/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "On market days, traders came from far away; the best stalls went to the first."
msgstr ""
"Les jours de marché, les marchands venaient de loin ; les meilleurs étals revenaient aux premiers "
"arrivés."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
