#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Mill Turns"
msgstr "Le moulin tourne"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The harvest is in, and the mill wheel turns day and night! But the farmers are slow. Bring me six "
"crates of grain to grind."
msgstr ""
"La moisson est rentrée, et la roue du moulin tourne jour et nuit ! Mais les fermiers sont lents. "
"{crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-moi six caisses de grain à moudre."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six crates! Listen to the stones grind. Bjarne says hello, and here is your share."
msgstr ""
"Six caisses ! {crew|Écoute|Écoute|Écoutez} les meules tourner. Bjarne {crew|te|te|vous} dit "
"bonjour, et voici {crew|ta|ta|votre} part."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Most vikings ground their grain by hand with two stones; a water mill was a wonder."
msgstr ""
"La plupart des Vikings moulaient leur grain à la main avec deux pierres ; un moulin à eau était "
"une merveille."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Henhouse Full"
msgstr "Un poulailler plein"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eggs sell so well! Let us have six hens. Buy hens at the market in Kråkhamn or the farm of "
"Frosttorp, and bring them home."
msgstr ""
"Les œufs se vendent si bien ! Prenons six poules. {crew|Achète|Achète|Achetez} des poules au "
"marché de Kråkhamn ou à la ferme de Frosttorp, et {crew|ramène|ramène|ramenez}-les à la maison."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six hens! Cluck, cluck, scratch, scratch. Do not forget: they eat grain."
msgstr ""
"Six poules ! Cot, cot, gratte, gratte. N'{crew|oublie|oublie|oubliez} pas : elles mangent du "
"grain."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking hens were small and laid fewer eggs than ours, but every farm had some."
msgstr ""
"Les poules vikings étaient petites et pondaient moins d'œufs que les nôtres, mais chaque ferme en "
"avait."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey Cakes"
msgstr "Les gâteaux au miel"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We want to sell honey cakes on the market! But we have no oven. Bring honey and grain to your "
"grandmother; she bakes them overnight, and you bring us the cakes."
msgstr ""
"On veut vendre des gâteaux au miel au marché ! Mais on n'a pas de four. "
"{crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez} du miel et du grain à {crew|ta|ta|votre} grand-mère ; elle les "
"fait cuire pendant la nuit, et {crew|tu nous apportes|tu nous apportes|vous nous apportez} les "
"gâteaux."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey! Now the grain."
msgstr "Du miel ! Maintenant, le grain."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "I bake them tonight. Come for them in the morning!"
msgstr "Je les fais cuire cette nuit. {crew|Viens|Viens|Venez} les chercher demain matin !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Still warm. Do not eat them all on the way!"
msgstr "Encore chauds. Ne les {crew|mange|mange|mangez} pas tous en route !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "They smell so good! Everybody comes to our stall. Here, half the silver is yours."
msgstr ""
"Ils sentent si bon ! Tout le monde vient à notre étal. {crew|Tiens|Tiens|Tenez}, la moitié de "
"l'argent est pour {crew|toi|toi|vous}."

