#, fuzzy
msgid "The Chieftain's Feast"
msgstr "La fête du chef"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My daughter Thora turns twelve! A feast with the whole valley: bring me three crates of mead and "
"two of cheese, within three days."
msgstr ""
"Ma fille Thora va avoir douze ans ! Une fête avec toute la vallée : "
"{crew|apporte|apporte|apportez}-moi trois caisses d'hydromel et deux de fromage, en trois jours."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The mead! The skalds will sing."
msgstr "L'hydromel ! Les scaldes vont chanter."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese, mead, songs and a fire! Come in, sit by me: it is the best birthday ever."
msgstr ""
"Du fromage, de l'hydromel, des chansons et un feu ! {crew|Entre|Entre|Entrez}, {crew|assieds-"
"toi|assieds-toi|asseyez-vous} près de moi : c'est le plus bel anniversaire de tous."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A chieftain's hall had a long fire in the middle, and benches along the walls."
msgstr "La halle d'un chef avait un long feu au milieu, et des bancs le long des murs."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ferryman's Tale"
msgstr "L'histoire du passeur"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Old Halvard told a story here last night: a hidden cove, where the swans of the lakes are born. He"
" says: ask the potter, the miller and the old man of Svanetorp."
msgstr ""
"Le vieux Halvard a raconté une histoire ici hier soir : une crique cachée, où naissent les cygnes "
"des lacs. Il dit : {crew|demande|demande|demandez} à la potière, à la meunière et au vieux de "
"Svanetorp."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cove? My grandmother said: it lies where the reeds grow tallest. Ask Astrid."
msgstr ""
"La crique ? Ma grand-mère disait : elle est là où les roseaux poussent le plus haut. "
"{crew|Demande|Demande|Demandez} à Astrid."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Reeds? The tallest ones grow south, by Svanetorp. Go to Grim."
msgstr ""
"Des roseaux ? Les plus hauts poussent au sud, près de Svanetorp. {crew|Va|Va|Allez} voir Grim."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So you found my secret. Behind my farm, in the reeds: the swan cove. Look, the cygnets! Grey and "
"fluffy. Tell no one!"
msgstr ""
"Alors {crew|tu as|tu as|vous avez} trouvé mon secret. Derrière ma ferme, dans les roseaux : la "
"crique des cygnes. {crew|Regarde|Regarde|Regardez}, les petits ! Gris et tout duveteux. Ne le "
"{crew|dis|dis|dites} à personne !"

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr "le secret de la crique des cygnes"

#. the thing 'the secret of the swan cove' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the
#. direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Young swans are grey, not white; they are called cygnets."
msgstr "Les jeunes cygnes sont gris, pas blancs ; on les appelle des cygneaux."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool for the Winter Cloth"
msgstr "De la laine pour l'hiver"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Everybody wants warm cloth for the winter, and my looms are hungry. Bring me four crates of wool, "
"and I give you a bolt of red cloth."
msgstr ""
"Tout le monde veut du tissu chaud pour l'hiver, et mes métiers à tisser ont faim. "
"{crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-moi quatre caisses de laine, et je {crew|te|te|vous} donne un "
"rouleau de tissu rouge."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clack, clack, goes the loom. Here: the reddest cloth I ever made, for you."
msgstr ""
"Clac, clac, fait le métier. {crew|Tiens|Tiens|Tenez} : le tissu le plus rouge que j'aie jamais "
"fait, pour {crew|toi|toi|vous}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The women of a viking farm wove all the cloth: sails, clothes and blankets."
msgstr "Les femmes d'une ferme viking tissaient tout : les voiles, les habits et les couvertures."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax in the Field"
msgstr "Du lin dans le champ"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Linen is softer than wool on the skin. Plant flax on your farm! When it blooms blue and is ripe, "
"bring me two crates."
msgstr ""
"Le lin est plus doux que la laine sur la peau. {crew|Sème|Sème|Semez} du lin à la ferme ! Quand il"
" fleurit en bleu et qu'il est mûr, {crew|apporte|apporte|apportez}-m'en deux caisses."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax seed in the field. In a few days, it blooms blue."
msgstr "Des graines de lin dans le champ. Dans quelques jours, il fleurira en bleu."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Your own flax! I will make you linen shirts, soft as a cloud."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Ton|Ton|Votre} propre lin ! Je vais {crew|te|te|vous} faire des chemises de lin, douces "
"comme un nuage."

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr "des chemises de lin"

#. the thing 'linen shirts' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax was soaked, beaten and combed for weeks before it could be spun into linen."
msgstr "Le lin trempait, était battu et peigné pendant des semaines avant d'être filé."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley for the Brewer"
msgstr "De l'orge pour le brasseur"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Orm of Hallvik wants the biggest barrel of ale for the autumn feast. I need grain, five crates! "
"Bring them, and you get two crates of my ale."
msgstr ""
"Orm de Hallvik veut le plus grand tonneau de bière pour la fête d'automne. Il me faut du grain, "
"cinq caisses ! {crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-les, et {crew|tu auras|tu auras|vous aurez} deux "
"caisses de ma bière."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Into the water with it, let it sprout... In a week, the best ale of the lakes!"
msgstr "Dans l'eau, on le laisse germer... Dans une semaine, la meilleure bière des lacs !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale was brewed from barley and water, often with herbs instead of hops."
msgstr ""
"La bière était brassée avec de l'orge et de l'eau, souvent avec des herbes au lieu du houblon."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Proper Hold"
msgstr "Une vraie cale"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You are real traders now: you need a real hold! Bring me eight planks from Frosttorp and two "
"crates of iron tools, and pay 20 silver. Then your hold takes two more crates."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Tu es un vrai marchand|Tu es une vraie marchande|Vous êtes de vrais marchands|Vous êtes de "
"vraies marchandes} maintenant : il {crew|te|te|vous} faut une vraie cale ! "
"{crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-moi huit planches de Frosttorp et deux caisses d'outils en fer, et"
" {crew|paie|paie|payez} 20 pièces d'argent. Alors {crew|ta|ta|votre} cale prendra deux caisses de "
"plus."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Planks of pine, split with wedges. Stack them well!"
msgstr "Des planches de pin, fendues avec des coins. {crew|Empile|Empile|Empilez}-les bien !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good iron! Now my wages."
msgstr "Bon fer ! Maintenant, mon salaire."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Saw, plane, rivets... Look at her! Longer, wider, and room for two more crates."
msgstr ""
"Scie, rabot, rivets... {crew|Regarde|Regarde|Regardez}-le ! Plus long, plus large, et de la place "
"pour deux caisses de plus."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Plank"
msgstr "Planche"

