#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking boats were built of overlapping planks, held with iron rivets."
msgstr ""
"Les bateaux vikings étaient faits de planches qui se chevauchaient, tenues par des rivets de fer."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Messenger's Cold"
msgstr "Le rhume de la messagère"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Atchoo! I have a cold, and I must tell the smith, the horse farm and the herders about the autumn "
"feast at Hallvik. Can you do it today? Atchoo!"
msgstr ""
"Atchoum ! J'ai un rhume, et je dois parler de la fête d'automne de Hallvik au forgeron, au haras "
"et aux bergers. {crew|Tu peux|Tu peux|Vous pouvez} le faire aujourd'hui ? Atchoum !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The autumn feast? I will bring my best knives to show."
msgstr "La fête d'automne ? J'apporterai mes plus beaux couteaux à montrer."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "We will come with all the horses! Tell Inga to drink hot honey water."
msgstr ""
"On viendra avec tous les chevaux ! {crew|Dis|Dis|Dites} à Inga de boire de l'eau chaude au miel."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A feast! I will bring my flute. Thank you!"
msgstr "Une fête ! J'apporterai ma flûte. Merci !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Messengers rowed, rode and ran: news could cross a land in a few days."
msgstr ""
"Les messagers ramaient, chevauchaient et couraient : une nouvelle pouvait traverser un pays en "
"quelques jours."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for Frosttorp"
msgstr "Du foin pour Frosttorp"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hay meadow was flooded, and the cows are hungry! I need eight crates of hay. Your big boat can "
"do it in one trip."
msgstr ""
"Ma prairie a été inondée, et les vaches ont faim ! Il me faut huit caisses de foin. "
"{crew|Ton|Ton|Votre} grand bateau peut le faire en un seul voyage."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Moo! Listen to them, they are happy. You saved my winter. Take this cheese."
msgstr ""
"Meuh ! {crew|Écoute|Écoute|Écoutez}-les, elles sont contentes. {crew|Tu as|Tu as|Vous avez} sauvé "
"mon hiver. {crew|Prends|Prends|Prenez} ce fromage."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay is dried grass; without enough of it, a farm could not keep its animals over winter."
msgstr ""
"Le foin, c'est de l'herbe séchée ; sans assez de foin, une ferme ne pouvait pas garder ses animaux"
" l'hiver."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's Cheese"
msgstr "Le fromage de Sigvor"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My goats gave so much milk this summer! I made four big wheels of cheese for Orm's autumn feast in"
" Hallvik, but my boat is full of goats. Will you carry them?"
msgstr ""
"Mes chèvres ont donné tant de lait cet été ! J'ai fait quatre grosses meules de fromage pour la "
"fête d'automne d'Orm, à Hallvik, mais mon bateau est plein de chèvres. {crew|Tu veux|Tu veux|Vous "
"voulez} bien les porter ?"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's cheese! The guests will fight over it. Well, not fight: they will ask nicely."
msgstr ""
"Le fromage de Sigvor ! Les invités vont se battre pour l'avoir. Enfin, pas se battre : ils "
"demanderont gentiment."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Roll them in gently. And no nibbling!"
msgstr "{crew|Fais|Fais|Faites}-les rouler doucement à bord. Et on ne grignote pas !"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese"
msgstr "Fromage"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}"
msgstr "{count|une meule de fromage|{count} meules de fromage}"

#. the thing '{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese keeps the milk of the summer for the winter."
msgstr "Le fromage garde le lait de l'été pour l'hiver."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow of Our Own"
msgstr "Une vache à nous"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the east meadow, we have room for a cow at last! Buy one at the horse farm in Torsgården. A "
"cow is big, but she fits in your boat like a crate, if she stands still."
msgstr ""
"Avec le pré de l'est, on a enfin de la place pour une vache ! {crew|Achète|Achète|Achetez}-en une "
"au haras de Torsgården. Une vache, c'est gros, mais elle tient dans {crew|ton|ton|votre} bateau "
"comme une caisse, si elle reste tranquille."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look at her big brown eyes! She will give us milk every day. Let us call her Rosa."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Regarde|Regarde|Regardez} ses grands yeux marron ! Elle nous donnera du lait tous les jours."
" Appelons-la Rosa."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cows were the wealth of a farm: a family counted its riches in cows."
msgstr "Les vaches étaient la richesse d'une ferme : une famille comptait sa fortune en vaches."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots for Ekvik"
msgstr "Des pots pour Ekvik"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fish soup! We cook it for the whole village, but our big pot cracked. Bring us three crates of"
" pots from the potter, please."
msgstr ""
"La soupe de poisson ! On la fait pour tout le village, mais notre grande marmite s'est fendue. "
"{crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-nous trois caisses de pots de chez la potière, s'il "
"{crew|te|te|vous} plaît."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New pots! Tonight there is fish soup for everybody, and for you two the first bowl."
msgstr ""
"Des pots neufs ! Ce soir, il y a de la soupe de poisson pour tout le monde, et pour "
"{crew|toi|toi|vous deux} le premier bol."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cooking pot hung over the fire on a chain, and the soup simmered all day."
msgstr "La marmite pendait au-dessus du feu à une chaîne, et la soupe mijotait toute la journée."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ragna's Broken Oar"
msgstr "La rame cassée de Ragna"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ragna rowed out at dawn and is not back! I fear her oar broke. Find her on the lakes, then come "
"back and fetch the spare oar for her."
msgstr ""
"Ragna est partie ramer à l'aube et elle n'est pas rentrée ! J'ai peur que sa rame soit cassée. "
"{crew|Trouve|Trouve|Trouvez}-la sur les lacs, puis {crew|reviens|reviens|revenez} chercher la rame"
" de rechange pour elle."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hello! Yes, my oar broke, and I drift with one. Tell Tor to give you the spare one!"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour ! Oui, ma rame est cassée, et je dérive avec une seule. {crew|Dis|Dis|Dites} à Tor de "
"{crew|te|te|vous} donner celle de rechange !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "She is well? Thank the gods. Here is the oar: bring it to her!"
msgstr "Elle va bien ? Merci aux dieux. Voici la rame : {crew|apporte|apporte|apportez}-la-lui !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My oar! Now I can row again. Here, take some fish: the freshest on the lakes."
msgstr ""
"Ma rame ! Je peux ramer à nouveau. {crew|Tiens|Tiens|Tenez}, {crew|prends|prends|prenez} du "
"poisson : le plus frais des lacs."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every viking boat carried spare oars: a broken oar was common."
msgstr "Chaque bateau viking avait des rames de rechange : une rame cassée, ça arrivait souvent."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Torches for the Dark"
msgstr "Des torches pour la nuit"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The nights grow long. The guests of the autumn feast need light: bring me tar for torches, two "
"pots from Ekvik, and two crates of flax for the wicks."
msgstr ""
"Les nuits s'allongent. Les invités de la fête d'automne ont besoin de lumière : "
"{crew|apporte|apporte|apportez}-moi du goudron pour les torches, deux pots d'Ekvik, et deux "
"caisses de lin pour les mèches."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar for torches? They burn bright and long."
msgstr "Du goudron pour des torches ? Elles brûlent fort et longtemps."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar and flax: now my torches will light up the whole bay!"
msgstr "Du goudron et du lin : mes torches vont éclairer toute la baie !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking torches were sticks wrapped in flax or cloth, soaked in tar or fat."
msgstr ""
"Les torches vikings étaient des bâtons entourés de lin ou de tissu, trempés dans du goudron ou de "
"la graisse."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Autumn Feast"
msgstr "La fête d'automne"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The autumn feast is tomorrow! Knut's ale is ready, five barrels. Bring them from Lindtorp, and "
"bring three crates of fish for the soup too."
msgstr ""
"La fête d'automne, c'est demain ! La bière de Knut est prête, cinq tonneaux. {crew|Va|Va|Allez} "
"les chercher à Lindtorp, et {crew|apporte|apporte|apportez} aussi trois caisses de poisson pour la"
" soupe."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ale! Now the fish."
msgstr "La bière ! Maintenant, le poisson."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The biggest batch I ever brewed! Five barrels for Orm."
msgstr "Le plus gros brassin de ma vie ! Cinq tonneaux pour Orm."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale, soup, torches, Sten's flute and Hrafn's knives! Everybody is here. Dance with us!"
msgstr ""
"La bière, la soupe, les torches, la flûte de Sten et les couteaux de Hrafn ! Tout le monde est là."
" {crew|Danse|Danse|Dansez} avec nous !"

