#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The vikings loved songs and riddles; at a feast, everybody had to sing."
msgstr ""
"Les Vikings adoraient les chansons et les devinettes ; pendant une fête, tout le monde devait "
"chanter."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Geese for the Market"
msgstr "Des oies pour le marché"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The geese of Frosttorp are the fattest on the lakes. I want six for the market! Each goose takes a"
" crate, and they honk all the way."
msgstr ""
"Les oies de Frosttorp sont les plus grasses des lacs. J'en veux six pour le marché ! Chaque oie "
"prend une caisse, et elles cacardent tout le long du voyage."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six geese, and not one escaped! The market will be loud today."
msgstr "Six oies, et pas une ne s'est échappée ! Ça va faire du bruit au marché aujourd'hui."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honk! Honk! Hold on to your hats, girls."
msgstr ""
"Couac ! Couac ! {crew|Tiens bien ton chapeau, mon petit|Tiens bien ton chapeau, ma petite|Tenez "
"bien vos chapeaux, les enfants|Tenez bien vos chapeaux, les filles}."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goose"
