#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runestones were raised for loved ones, and painted in bright colours."
msgstr ""
"On dressait les pierres runiques pour ceux qu'on aimait, et on les peignait de couleurs vives."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The First Snow"
msgstr "La première neige"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Snowflakes! Winter is near. Our store needs feed for the animals: six crates of hay and four of "
"grain. Your hold takes eight: think how to row it!"
msgstr ""
"Des flocons ! L'hiver approche. La réserve a besoin de fourrage pour les animaux : six caisses de "
"foin et quatre de grain. {crew|Ta|Ta|Votre} cale en prend huit : "
"{crew|réfléchis|réfléchis|réfléchissez} à la façon de tout rapporter !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for the sheep, the goats and Rosa. Now the grain."
msgstr "Du foin pour les moutons, les chèvres et Rosa. Maintenant, le grain."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The store is full! Let the snow come. Come in, the soup is hot."
msgstr ""
"La réserve est pleine ! La neige peut venir. {crew|Entre|Entre|Entrez}, la soupe est chaude."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "In winter, the animals stayed in the barn for months and ate the hay of the summer."
msgstr "En hiver, les animaux restaient des mois dans l'étable et mangeaient le foin de l'été."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ice Breaks"
msgstr "La glace se brise"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Hear that crack? The ice breaks: spring is here again! Row out and hail two boats: ask how "
"everybody got through the winter."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Tu entends|Tu entends|Vous entendez} ce craquement ? La glace se brise : le printemps est "
"revenu ! {crew|Sors|Sors|Sortez} ramer et {crew|salue|salue|saluez} deux bateaux : "
"{crew|demande|demande|demandez} comment chacun a passé l'hiver."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everybody is well! But Tova has asked for you all winter. Row to Laxön!"
msgstr ""
"Tout le monde va bien ! Mais Tova {crew|t'a réclamé|t'a réclamée|vous a réclamés|vous a réclamées}"
" tout l'hiver. {crew|Rame|Rame|Ramez} jusqu'à Laxön !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A long winter! But the herring kept, thanks to your salt."
msgstr "Un long hiver ! Mais les harengs se sont gardés, grâce à {crew|ton|ton|votre} sel."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There you are! Spring is when the animals need us most. Will you be my apprentices, and learn to "
"heal?"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Te|Te|Vous} voilà ! Au printemps, les animaux ont le plus besoin de nous. {crew|Veux-tu être"
" mon apprenti|Veux-tu être mon apprentie|Voulez-vous être mes apprentis|Voulez-vous être mes "
"apprenties}, pour apprendre à soigner ?"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the ice broke in spring, the boats came out, and with them the news."
msgstr "Quand la glace se brisait au printemps, les bateaux sortaient, et avec eux les nouvelles."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Coughing Horse"
msgstr "Le cheval qui tousse"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Your first case as healers: Ragnfrid's old horse Bror coughs. Take him this syrup of thyme and "
"honey, then come back to me after a night, to hear how he is."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Ton premier cas de guérisseur|Ton premier cas de guérisseuse|Votre premier cas de "
"guérisseurs|Votre premier cas de guérisseuses} : Bror, le vieux cheval de Ragnfrid, tousse. "
"{crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-lui ce sirop de thym et de miel, puis "
"{crew|reviens|reviens|revenez} me voir après une nuit, pour savoir comment il va."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thyme and honey? Bror loves it. He licks the spoon!"
msgstr "Du thym et du miel ? Bror adore ça. Il lèche la cuillère !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "He slept the whole night and coughs no more. Tell Tova: her apprentices are good!"
msgstr ""
"Il a dormi toute la nuit et ne tousse plus. {crew|Dis|Dis|Dites} à Tova : {crew|son apprenti est "
"doué|son apprentie est douée|ses apprentis sont doués|ses apprenties sont douées} !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Well done! You listened, you waited, you looked. That is healing."
msgstr ""
"Bravo ! {crew|Tu as écouté, tu as attendu, tu as regardé|Tu as écouté, tu as attendu, tu as "
"regardé|Vous avez écouté, vous avez attendu, vous avez regardé}. C'est ça, soigner."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Syrup"
msgstr "Sirop"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
