#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Silke's colt ran into the bog and is stuck to his belly! I need a long rope: Tor in Stormvik has "
"the longest. Hurry, he is scared!"
msgstr ""
"Le poulain de Silke a couru dans le marais et il est enfoncé jusqu'au ventre ! Il me faut une "
"longue corde : Tor, à Stormvik, a la plus longue. {crew|Dépêche-toi|Dépêche-toi|Dépêchez-vous}, il"
" a peur !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rope around him, gently, everybody pull... Slurp! He is out! Muddy, but well. You saved him."
msgstr ""
"La corde autour de lui, doucement, tout le monde tire... Floc ! Il est sorti ! Plein de boue, mais"
" il va bien. {crew|Tu l'as|Tu l'as|Vous l'avez} sauvé."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My longest rope! Take it, quick!"
msgstr "Ma plus longue corde ! {crew|Prends|Prends|Prenez}-la, vite !"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rope"
msgstr "Corde"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the long rope"
msgstr "la longue corde"

#. the thing 'the long rope' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct
#. object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the long rope"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A horse stuck in mud must be pulled out slowly, or it hurts its legs."
msgstr "Un cheval coincé dans la boue doit être tiré doucement, sinon il se blesse les pattes."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Grain for the North"
msgstr "Du grain pour le Nord"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hunters send news: the summer in the north was cold, and their families have no grain. My ship "
"leaves in three days: fill it with twelve crates!"
msgstr ""
"Mes chasseurs envoient des nouvelles : l'été dans le Nord a été froid, et leurs familles n'ont "
"plus de grain. Mon navire part dans trois jours : {crew|remplis|remplis|remplissez}-le de douze "
"caisses !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve crates! Nobody in the north goes hungry this winter. The whole valley thanks you."
msgstr ""
"Douze caisses ! Personne n'aura faim dans le Nord cet hiver. Toute la vallée {crew|te|te|vous} "
"remercie."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the harvest failed, the farms helped each other: next year, it might be them."
msgstr ""
"Quand la récolte était mauvaise, les fermes s'entraidaient : l'année suivante, ce serait peut-être"
" leur tour."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Wool Fair"
msgstr "La foire à la laine"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The wool fair! Traders come from the Long Lake to buy. Bring me eight crates of wool, the more the"
" better, and the fair is a success."
msgstr ""
"La foire à la laine ! Des marchands viennent du Long Lac pour acheter. "
"{crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-moi huit caisses de laine, et plus il y en a, mieux c'est : la "
"foire sera un succès."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eight crates! The traders from the Long Lake ask: who are these girls? I say: the best traders of "
"the Home Lakes."
msgstr ""
"Huit caisses ! Les marchands du Long Lac demandent : {crew|qui est ce garçon|qui est cette "
"fille|qui sont ces enfants|qui sont ces filles} ? Je réponds : {crew|le meilleur marchand|la "
"meilleure marchande|les meilleurs marchands|les meilleures marchandes} des Lacs du Foyer."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool was so important that some sagas tell of whole ships full of it."
msgstr ""
"La laine était si importante que certaines sagas parlent de navires entiers remplis de laine."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Goats on the Island"
msgstr "Les chèvres sur l'île"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My four goats swam to Bergö! They eat Dagny's flowers, and she is cross. Bring them back before "
"they eat her kiln too!"
msgstr ""
"Mes quatre chèvres ont nagé jusqu'à Bergö ! Elles mangent les fleurs de Dagny, et elle est fâchée."
" {crew|Ramène|Ramène|Ramenez}-les avant qu'elles mangent aussi son four !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My naughty goats! Tomorrow I build a higher fence. Here, my best cheese."
msgstr ""
"Mes vilaines chèvres ! Demain, je construis une clôture plus haute. {crew|Tiens|Tiens|Tenez}, mon "
"meilleur fromage."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take them, take them! They ate my flowers and a basket and a shoe!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Prends|Prends|Prenez}-les, {crew|prends|prends|prenez}-les ! Elles ont mangé mes fleurs, un "
"panier et une chaussure !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goats are good swimmers when they must be, and they eat nearly anything."
msgstr "Les chèvres nagent bien quand il le faut, et elles mangent presque n'importe quoi."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "News for Everybody"
msgstr "Des nouvelles pour tous"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Big news: a ship from the Long Lake will come, and the way between the lakes opens! Tell the "
"smith, the fishers of Stormvik and Orm in Hallvik. I tell the rest."
msgstr ""
"Grande nouvelle : un navire du Long Lac va venir, et le passage entre les lacs s'ouvre ! "
"{crew|Préviens|Préviens|Prévenez} le forgeron, les pêcheurs de Stormvik et Orm, à Hallvik. Je "
"préviens les autres."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ship from the Long Lake? They will want my iron!"
msgstr "Un navire du Long Lac ? Ils vont vouloir mon fer !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New lakes, new fish! Thank you for telling us."
msgstr "De nouveaux lacs, de nouveaux poissons ! Merci de nous avoir prévenus."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Guests from far away! I must brew more. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr ""
"Des invités de très loin ! Je dois brasser plus. Merci, {crew|mon petit|ma petite|les enfants|les "
"filles} !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The lakes of the north were joined by rivers and portages, where boats were dragged over land."
msgstr ""
"Les lacs du Nord étaient reliés par des rivières et des portages, où l'on tirait les bateaux sur "
"la terre."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow for Grim"
msgstr "Une vache pour Grim"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I am old, and I would like fresh milk every morning. Bring me a cow from the horse farm. The swans"
" will be jealous!"
msgstr ""
"Je suis vieux, et j'aimerais du lait frais tous les matins. {crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-moi "
"une vache du haras. Les cygnes vont être jaloux !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A cow! I call her Swan, ha. Here, for your trouble, and for all the years you visited an old man."
msgstr ""
"Une vache ! Je l'appelle Cygne, ha. {crew|Tiens|Tiens|Tenez}, pour {crew|ta|ta|votre} peine, et "
"pour toutes ces années où {crew|tu es venu voir|tu es venue voir|vous êtes venus voir|vous êtes "
"venues voir} un vieil homme."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good cow gave milk for ten years or more, and was part of the family."
msgstr "Une bonne vache donnait du lait pendant dix ans ou plus, et faisait partie de la famille."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flowers on the Hill"
msgstr "Des fleurs sur la colline"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Plant flowers on the sunny hill! When they bloom, bring three crates to Gudrun's inn: she wants "
"the inn to smell like summer."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Sème|Sème|Semez} des fleurs sur la colline au soleil ! Quand elles fleurissent, "
"{crew|apporte|apporte|apportez} trois caisses à l'auberge de Gudrun : elle veut que l'auberge "
"sente l'été."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flower seeds in the earth. In two days, they bloom."
msgstr "Des graines de fleurs dans la terre. Dans deux jours, elles fleuriront."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Flowers on every table! The guests smile. Here is your silver, and a cup of milk for each of you."
msgstr ""
"Des fleurs sur chaque table ! Les clients sourient. Voici {crew|ton|ton|votre} argent, et une "
"tasse de lait pour {crew|toi|toi|chacun de vous|chacune de vous}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings wove flowers into wreaths and crowns for feasts and weddings."
msgstr "Les Vikings tressaient des fleurs en couronnes pour les fêtes et les mariages."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pottery Market"
msgstr "Le marché aux poteries"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The new kiln makes so many pots! Bring ten crates to the market in Kråkhamn. Ten crates: only your"
" big boat can do it."
msgstr ""
"Le nouveau four fait tant de pots ! {crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez} dix caisses au marché de "
"Kråkhamn. Dix caisses : seul {crew|ton|ton|votre} grand bateau peut le faire."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ten crates of Dagny's pots, and not one broken! The best rowing of the lakes."
msgstr "Dix caisses de pots de Dagny, et pas un seul cassé ! Le plus beau coup de rame des lacs."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pack them in straw: pots do not like to bump!"
msgstr "{crew|Emballe|Emballe|Emballez}-les dans la paille : les pots n'aiment pas les chocs !"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots"
msgstr "Pots"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}"
msgstr "{count|une caisse de pots|{count} caisses de pots}"

#. the thing '{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}' for {thing@acc} in the translations:
#. the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the
#. same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clay pots were carried packed in straw, so that they did not break."
msgstr "Les pots en argile voyageaient emballés dans la paille, pour ne pas se casser."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Gudrun's Ring"
msgstr "La bague de Gudrun"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My mother's ring! It slipped from my finger into the lake, by the jetty. Gone forever... unless a "
"fisher's net caught it? Ask Ragna."
msgstr ""
"La bague de ma mère ! Elle a glissé de mon doigt dans le lac, près du ponton. Perdue pour "
"toujours... sauf si le filet d'un pêcheur l'a attrapée ? {crew|Demande|Demande|Demandez} à Ragna."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ring? Wait... Tor found something shiny in our net yesterday! Ask him in Stormvik."
msgstr ""
"Une bague ? {crew|Attends|Attends|Attendez}... Tor a trouvé quelque chose de brillant dans notre "
"filet hier ! {crew|Demande|Demande|Demandez}-lui, à Stormvik."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My mother's ring! Back from the lake! I can not thank you enough. Every meal at my inn is free for"
" you."
msgstr ""
"La bague de ma mère ! Revenue du lac ! Je ne sais pas comment {crew|te|te|vous} remercier. Tous "
"les repas de mon auberge sont gratuits pour {crew|toi|toi|vous}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "This? Silver with a little red stone. I thought it was a fish's treasure!"
msgstr ""
"Ça ? De l'argent avec une petite pierre rouge. Je croyais que c'était le trésor d'un poisson !"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ring"
msgstr "Bague"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the ring"
msgstr "la bague"

#. the thing 'the ring' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the ring"
msgstr ""

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "free meals at the inn of Vargvik"
msgstr "des repas gratuits à l'auberge de Vargvik"

#. the thing 'free meals at the inn of Vargvik' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative
#. (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the
#. plain translation
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "free meals at the inn of Vargvik"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings sometimes gave silver to the lakes on purpose, as gifts to the gods."
msgstr "Les Vikings donnaient parfois de l'argent aux lacs exprès, en cadeau aux dieux."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Edge of the Forest"
msgstr "L'orée du bois"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kol and Ingrid want sheep for their new home. Bring them two sheep, and I give you the strip of "
"land by the forest, next to your farm. A fair trade!"
msgstr ""
"Kol et Ingrid veulent des moutons pour leur nouvelle maison. {crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez}-leur "
"deux moutons, et je {crew|te|te|vous} donne la bande de terre près de la forêt, à côté de "
"{crew|ta|ta|votre} ferme. Un échange honnête !"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two sheep for the young ones! Ingrid already knits. The forest edge is yours: good wood and two "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"Deux moutons pour les jeunes mariés ! Ingrid tricote déjà. L'orée du bois est à "
"{crew|toi|toi|vous} : du bon bois et deux champs."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Land was traded for animals, silver or work: there were no banks."
msgstr ""
"On échangeait la terre contre des animaux, de l'argent ou du travail : il n'y avait pas de "
"banques."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Longhouse Grows"
msgstr "La grande maison s'agrandit"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With so many animals and friends, our house is too small! Bring twelve logs from Frosttorp, two "
"crates of tools and two pots of tar, and we make it longer."
msgstr ""
"Avec tant d'animaux et d'amis, notre maison est trop petite ! {crew|Apporte|Apporte|Apportez} "
"douze rondins de Frosttorp, deux caisses d'outils et deux pots de goudron, et on l'allongera."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve logs! Fill that big hold of yours."
msgstr "Douze rondins ! {crew|Remplis|Remplis|Remplissez} {crew|ta|ta|votre} grande cale."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Axes and nails. Now the tar for the roof."
msgstr "Des haches et des clous. Maintenant, le goudron pour le toit."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hammering all night with the neighbours... Our longhouse is twice as long! Room for a feast."
msgstr ""
"On a martelé toute la nuit avec les voisins... Notre grande maison est deux fois plus longue ! "
"Assez de place pour une fête."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A longhouse could be made longer by adding a piece at the end, like a train."
msgstr ""
"On pouvait allonger une grande maison viking en ajoutant un morceau au bout, comme un train."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Green Valley"
msgstr "La vallée verte"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You helped my valley all year. The green valley behind your farm has no owner: bring me two crates"
" of cloth and two of honey for the gods' feast, and it is yours."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Tu as|Tu as|Vous avez} aidé ma vallée toute l'année. La vallée verte derrière "
"{crew|ta|ta|votre} ferme n'a pas de propriétaire : {crew|apporte|apporte|apportez}-moi deux "
"caisses de tissu et deux de miel pour la fête des dieux, et elle est à {crew|toi|toi|vous}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloth for the hall. Now the honey."
msgstr "Du tissu pour la halle. Maintenant, le miel."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Father says it at the Thing, in front of everybody: the green valley belongs to Ylva and Sigrid!"
msgstr "Papa le dit au Thing, devant tout le monde : la vallée verte appartient à Ylva et Sigrid !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At the Thing, the meeting of the free people, land and laws were decided."
msgstr "Au Thing, l'assemblée des gens libres, on décidait des terres et des lois."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bees for the Valley"
msgstr "Des abeilles pour la vallée"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The valley is full of clover and heather. Bees would love it! Have three beehives on the farm, and"
" we will have honey all year."
msgstr ""
"La vallée est pleine de trèfle et de bruyère. Les abeilles vont adorer ! Il {crew|te|te|vous} faut"
" trois ruches à la ferme, et on aura du miel toute l'année."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hum, hum, hum! Three hives in the valley. Honey for us, and for mead."
msgstr "Bzz, bzz, bzz ! Trois ruches dans la vallée. Du miel pour nous, et pour l'hydromel."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Heather honey is dark and strong; clover honey is light and mild."
msgstr "Le miel de bruyère est foncé et fort ; le miel de trèfle est clair et doux."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Apples for the Market"
msgstr "Des pommes pour le marché"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
